{title: Down by the Riverside}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - keeping the pulse through three chords}
{artist: Traditional African American spiritual}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}
{tag: beginner, spiritual, three chords}
# Traditional public-domain text; selected sword-and-shield and burden verses.
# Fresh simplified accompaniment; see README.md for text and history sources.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Keep the same pulse in verse and chorus. Practise F to C separately first.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Gonna [C]lay down my sword and shield, down by the riverside,
[G7]Down by the riverside, [C]down by the riverside;
Gonna [C]lay down my sword and shield, down by the riverside,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I ain't gonna [F]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [C]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
I ain't gonna [F]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [C]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Gonna [C]lay down my burden, down by the riverside,
[G7]Down by the riverside, [C]down by the riverside;
Gonna [C]lay down my burden, down by the riverside,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I ain't gonna [F]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [C]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
I ain't gonna [F]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [C]study war no more,
I ain't gonna [G7]study war no [C]more.
{end_of_chorus}
